WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.680
Modern life is a disease. [music] You

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:09.040
want to get ahead. So why do you always

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:12.080
feel behind? You want to be useful. So

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.960
why do you feel unseen? The problem

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.080
isn't you? Modern life is like a Trojan

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.400
horse that arrives as a gift and then

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.960
takes over from the inside. [music]

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.240
I've lived as a monk in training, as a

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:29.359
Wall Street banker, as a CEO and I found

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.480
the same exact pattern everywhere. There

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:35.920
are four symptoms, but one of them is

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.000
probably ruining your life or even

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.840
ruining it. So, by the end of this

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.440
video, you'll know all four of those

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.000
symptoms and what [music] to do about

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.879
each of them. Let's get started. The

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.920
hardest thing about modern life is how

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:52.480
everyone wants to make your life easier.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.039
We have infinite feed, infinite

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.000
calories, infinite streaming. Yes,

00:00:55.039 --> 00:01:01.359
somehow we're the ones being consumed.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.120
I'll give you my own example. I had a

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:04.960
clear [music] vision of success when I

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.360
was young. Walking out of Penn Station

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:11.119
in New York City, I'm wearing a crisp

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:14.000
suit and I'm entering a marble lobby of

00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:15.760
a top investment bank. And I got there,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.360
you [music] know, it was the right suit,

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:22.320
the right lobby. But today, all I

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.560
remember now is that I was sitting at a

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.439
desk for 18 hours, eating [music]

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.320
takeout, staring at numbers at 1:00 in

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:34.000
the morning, sleeping for four or 5

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:37.439
hours, and on [music] repeat every day.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
I rarely saw my friends. I rarely saw

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:42.159
the sun. And that's the irony of modern

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.720
life. We're surrounded by comfort, but

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:48.000
we feel restless. [music] We now run

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:51.439
faster than ever, but we still feel

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.281
behind. We're connected, but we feel

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:57.280
alone. We wonder if anything we do

00:01:55.281 --> 00:02:00.159
[music] matters. These are the four

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.759
symptoms that I see everywhere I go.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:06.960
Restless,

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:09.280
behind, alone, unseen. The real irony of

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.400
modern life is that the dream and the

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.720
disease look exactly the same. And to

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.879
understand why that happens, we have to

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.000
start with these symptoms and dig into

00:02:16.879 --> 00:02:23.040
the root causes of each of them from the

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.640
inside. Let's do that. The first symptom

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:29.440
is us feeling restless and anxious. We

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.319
all live in this hustle and grind

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:35.599
culture. No one believes in stopping or

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:37.440
even slowing down. In 2018, a Harvard

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:41.131
Business School professor named Michael

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:44.400
Norton ran a study on more than 2,000

00:02:41.131 --> 00:02:47.840
[music] people. Every one of them had a

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.879
net worth of at least a million dollars.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.680
Lucky ducks. Many of them were actually

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:57.519
far beyond that. And he asked each one

00:02:53.680 --> 00:03:00.160
of them two questions. How happy are you

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:02.400
on a scale of 1 to 10? [music] and how

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.959
much more money would you need to move

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.680
your happiness to a 10? The second

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:10.720
question received the most [music]

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:14.159
interesting answer. The person with 1

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:16.400
million said they only needed [music] to

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:19.760
get to 3 million to get their happiness

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:22.080
to 10, but the person with 3 million

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.599
wanted 10 million [music] and the person

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:28.319
with 10 million wanted 30. No matter

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:30.799
where they were on the wealth chart,

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:34.400
they all wanted roughly three times

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:37.120
more. So, it's never about that number.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.840
No matter where you are, there's always

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:43.200
a bigger number. About a month ago, I

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:46.319
was talking to a 24 year old and I asked

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:49.200
him what do he wanted to be. His answer

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:52.720
was rich.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:56.080
That answer really surprised me because

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:57.760
I told him, you know, rich is not a

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:01.280
career.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.519
But that's interestingly the entire goal

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.239
for many people.

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:10.000
Chase the number first and then hope

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:13.599
that meaning will somehow arrive later.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.160
Our careers, our companies, our

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:19.519
relationships, we all do that. We're

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:24.240
incapable of feeling happy with what we

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:27.759
have or who we have. We feel restless

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:31.520
when we don't know our why behind the

00:04:27.759 --> 00:04:34.400
what. So, here's the action item. Take

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:37.120
the thing you're chasing right now and

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.720
ask, "What was it supposed to do for

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.960
you? What's that number for? Is it so

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.680
you can retire and you don't have to

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:48.240
work? Is it about safety? Is it about

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.720
security? Is it about a specific

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:53.520
lifestyle that you coveret? Is it about

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.120
giving your family and kids what you

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.080
didn't have? All those are great

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:01.040
reasons, but when you have that clarity,

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.040
it helps you become more restful. But

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.840
there is one more reason money can make

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.759
us all restless. When you don't know

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.120
exactly where you stand with your

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:14.800
finances, I had that problem. My

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:16.880
financial life was scattered everywhere.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:20.720
Old 401ks,

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:24.000
IRA, bank accounts, brokerage accounts,

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.960
credit card. So, my accountant suggested

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.680
Monarch [music]

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.680
and I started using that software and I

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.919
loved it. They're sponsoring this

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:34.880
segment, but I was already a customer

00:05:31.919 --> 00:05:37.440
before they leed out. Monarch pulled my

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:40.880
bank accounts, my investments, my credit

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:43.919
cards, my loans into one clean

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:46.800
dashboard. So instead of jumping across

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:49.759
10 different apps, I can see the full

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:53.039
financial picture in one place. It makes

00:05:49.759 --> 00:05:56.720
me feel very zen. If you know what you

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:59.199
have, what you spend, what you owe, the

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.759
financial fog starts to lift. [music]

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:03.600
And that matters because clarity creates

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:05.919
sanity. You can try it for free

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.160
yourself. The link is below. There's

00:06:05.919 --> 00:06:10.720
also a code to get half off your entire

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:14.800
first year. Now, let's go to the second

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:17.840
symptom, feeling behind. In 2019,

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:21.280
Instagram research team found that their

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:25.440
app was making body image issues even

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:29.039
worse for one in three teenage girls. In

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:33.440
2020, Instagram also found that those

00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:36.560
teenagers were especially vulnerable to

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:38.720
reward driven use and they had

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:42.319
difficulty stopping even when they

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:44.800
wanted to. So what did Instagram do?

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:48.319
Nothing much. The company did not

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:51.120
fundamentally redesign the product or

00:06:48.319 --> 00:06:54.000
even disclose the finding publicly until

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:57.120
they were leaked in 2021 by a

00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:00.080
whistleblower. The problem was that the

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:03.440
teenage girls who had body image issues

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:06.960
were constantly exposed to perfect

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:10.400
bodies. But it's a competition those

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:13.840
teenagers could never win. Being ahead

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:16.479
of everyone alive is an insane

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:19.919
condition. And like those teenagers,

00:07:16.479 --> 00:07:23.440
there is no version of your life or mine

00:07:19.919 --> 00:07:27.440
where nobody is looking better or doing

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:30.319
better than you and me. That's a game we

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.479
can never win. So we tell ourselves

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:36.240
stories about us falling behind because

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:40.800
we're not enough. I did that for so many

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:43.039
years. My dad and my aunts used to put

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:46.080
me down all the time when I was a little

00:07:43.039 --> 00:07:49.759
kid. They didn't like the way I wore my

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:53.680
glasses. I was too skinny. They made fun

00:07:49.759 --> 00:07:56.960
of my nose. And so I grew up with

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:59.520
serious body image issues. But you know

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.360
what? There is nothing wrong with my

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.919
nose

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:06.160
or with me. And there's nothing wrong

00:08:03.919 --> 00:08:08.879
with you.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.720
You are not behind or ahead. You're

00:08:08.879 --> 00:08:13.360
right where you are. That's what I

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:16.319
realized later on. We forget that yes,

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:19.039
success requires effort and yes, you

00:08:16.319 --> 00:08:21.840
have to run fast. But the folks who are

00:08:19.039 --> 00:08:24.080
ahead of you know that there are some

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:26.400
people ahead of them. Someone who's

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.400
faster or smarter is always going to

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:30.560
find someone faster and smarter. That's

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:33.200
just the way life works. You did not

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:36.800
choose your comparison set. Just like I

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:40.560
didn't choose my nose. It was there when

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:42.320
I was born. It was what you inherited.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:44.320
We'll talk about what to do about all of

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:47.760
that, but let's go to the third symptom

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:50.800
now. Feeling alone. When I was younger,

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:53.600
I co-ounded a band [music] with two of

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.920
my buddies. And we played hundreds of

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:58.000
concerts around the US, around the world

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:00.480
actually. But the part we looked forward

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:04.000
to the most was what happened after the

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:06.640
concert. We would stay up until 3 or 4

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:09.519
in the morning [music] and just talk. We

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:13.440
would talk about music, about poetry,

00:09:09.519 --> 00:09:16.800
about neuroscience, astronomy, religion,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:20.480
atheism, questions none of us had any

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:23.440
answers to. There was no audience,

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:26.000
just [music] us and our stories. And

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:28.640
those conversations are still what I

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.720
miss the most about demand.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:33.360
That's what modern life takes away from

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:36.800
us. It confuses us. There's nothing

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:40.560
social about social media. They're just

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:43.040
media platforms and algorithms who want

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:46.480
you to stay on them so they can show you

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:50.240
ads. Social media in fact makes you

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:53.120
antisocial in many ways. Look around any

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:55.680
elevator, any line, any train station,

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.839
any checkout, and you'll see every head

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:00.720
is down just looking at their phones.

00:09:57.839 --> 00:10:03.440
We're physically there, but our mind is

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.519
living somewhere else in that digital

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:08.000
world. But eventually, we come to

00:10:05.519 --> 00:10:10.480
realize that your thousand followers

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.399
cannot replace the one person you're

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.640
going to need who will sit down next to

00:10:12.399 --> 00:10:16.800
you when you're hurting. So, that's the

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:19.440
third symptom. And by the way, if you

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:22.560
like such ideas and frameworks, please

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:25.360
subscribe to my newsletter where we go

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:28.720
way deeper into these kind of topics.

