free. And you can also take this episode

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:39.360
with you on your morning run or commute

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:41.920
because you can follow it on Spotify

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:45.760
now, which is super cool. And now the

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:49.360
fourth symptom is familiar to all of us

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:52.640
and that is almost existential feeling

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:57.839
unseen and unappreciated.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:11:00.260
We all want to be wanted. We all want to

00:10:57.839 --> 00:11:00.880
know that something changed because

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:04.399
[music]

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:06.800
we were here. You want your boss to

00:11:04.399 --> 00:11:09.279
appreciate your work. You want your

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:11.279
spouse to pay [music] attention to you.

00:11:09.279 --> 00:11:13.200
You want your real or post to get

00:11:11.279 --> 00:11:17.519
eyeballs. You want your videos to go

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:21.040
viral. All of that is about our want to

00:11:17.519 --> 00:11:23.920
be seen. We all want to matter. And this

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:27.519
is also where AI creates the deepest

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:29.600
fear. For decades, we've worked on

00:11:27.519 --> 00:11:32.720
building our intelligence, our

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:35.600
expertise, so we can stand out, right?

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:38.240
So we can be seen. But AI can now

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:40.160
perform many of the skills we spent

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:43.440
years building. And it can do it

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:46.240
cheaper, faster, without getting tired.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.480
And it doesn't care about being seen. It

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:50.880
doesn't care about recognition. So what

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:54.399
happens to us when the skills that we

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:57.360
spend years building become suddenly

00:11:54.399 --> 00:12:02.160
commoditized? Are we just disposable

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:04.959
now? Will our value be repriced in the

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:08.079
market? No one knows the answer to those

00:12:04.959 --> 00:12:11.360
questions yet. No one will know for next

00:12:08.079 --> 00:12:13.519
5 years, I think. But that's why it

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:17.040
feels a little more personal and

00:12:13.519 --> 00:12:19.279
existential than it used to because AI

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.320
is this amplifier.

00:12:19.279 --> 00:12:25.040
So there they are, the four symptoms,

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:30.160
the feeling that you're restless,

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:33.519
behind, alone, and unseen. What's the

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:36.639
underlying root cause for all of them?

00:12:33.519 --> 00:12:40.000
There are many causes, but one key one

00:12:36.639 --> 00:12:43.279
that I think is that we tend to

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:45.519
substitute the real hero with a stunt

00:12:43.279 --> 00:12:48.240
double. And that's the problem. You

00:12:45.519 --> 00:12:50.639
measure the wrong metric, you drive

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.440
wrong behavior. There is a principle

00:12:50.639 --> 00:12:56.160
called Goodart's law. When a measure

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:58.959
itself becomes a target to optimize, it

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:01.839
stops being a a good measure. Our modern

00:12:58.959 --> 00:13:05.040
lives are full of those broken measures.

00:13:01.839 --> 00:13:09.279
Money is a stunt double for security and

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:12.399
freedom. A title is stunt double for

00:13:09.279 --> 00:13:15.519
being taken seriously. A company may be

00:13:12.399 --> 00:13:17.600
a proxy for building something that

00:13:15.519 --> 00:13:19.440
outlasts you.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.240
Now the stunt doubles are not

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:24.079
meaningless. Money matters. Cash flow

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:26.720
keeps your company alive. All that is

00:13:24.079 --> 00:13:30.160
good. But some of the stun doubles

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:33.680
become so convincing that we forget that

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:36.000
there is a hero that ever existed. So

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.399
that's the pattern and here's how you

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:42.320
break it. The disease called the modern

00:13:38.399 --> 00:13:45.760
life requires a four-step remedy and for

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:50.639
that we have to go back to the 70s. John

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:52.880
Bogle started Vanguard in 1970s and it

00:13:50.639 --> 00:13:55.760
became one of the largest financial

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:59.839
institutions in the world. It still is,

00:13:55.760 --> 00:14:03.120
but he gave it a structure that's almost

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:06.560
unheard of in finance. Vanguard would be

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:09.279
owned by its funds and those funds would

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:11.519
be owned by their investors. It still

00:14:09.279 --> 00:14:14.560
works that way. He built one of the

00:14:11.519 --> 00:14:17.279
largest financial firms in history and

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:20.240
never owned any equity in that company.

00:14:17.279 --> 00:14:24.000
He wasn't confused by the stunt doubles

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:27.279
and the fake measures. He knew the real

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:30.639
thing. So, how do we do the same? Here

00:14:27.279 --> 00:14:34.320
are the four steps. First, name the

00:14:30.639 --> 00:14:40.079
symptom. What are you actually feeling?

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:42.720
Restless, behind, alone, unseen. Now,

00:14:40.079 --> 00:14:45.360
this matters because you'll often

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:47.839
misdiagnose the real problem. So, for

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:50.810
example, when you say you need a

00:14:47.839 --> 00:14:51.440
promotion, are you feeling behind

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:57.760
[clears throat]

00:14:51.440 --> 00:15:00.000
or restless or unseen or all three? You

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:02.399
got to know the difference. Step two,

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.040
find the need that's underneath that

00:15:02.399 --> 00:15:10.800
symptom. Each symptom has an underlying

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:14.560
unspoken need. When you feel restless,

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:16.959
your underlying need might be safety.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:19.839
When you feel behind, your underlying

00:15:16.959 --> 00:15:23.839
need might be adequacy. When you feel

00:15:19.839 --> 00:15:26.959
alone, it could be belonging. When you

00:15:23.839 --> 00:15:29.199
feel unseen, your underlying need could

00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:31.839
be significance.

00:15:29.199 --> 00:15:34.639
So, go for a walk. Figure it out. Write

00:15:31.839 --> 00:15:37.279
it down. What is it that you truly need?

00:15:34.639 --> 00:15:39.920
Step number three, expose the stunt

00:15:37.279 --> 00:15:42.240
double. What proxy are you chasing

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:44.560
instead of that underlying need? Because

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:46.880
it's easier to measure the proxy.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:49.120
Followers can be counted. Belonging

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:51.519
cannot. You can measure how fast you're

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:54.240
running compared to your peers. But your

00:15:51.519 --> 00:15:57.360
own sense of satisfaction is hard to

00:15:54.240 --> 00:16:00.399
measure. The stunt double is attractive

00:15:57.360 --> 00:16:03.120
precisely because it gives you a score.

00:16:00.399 --> 00:16:06.000
It tells you whether the number went up

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:10.000
or down, but it cannot tell you whether

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:13.440
the real need has been met or not.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:16.480
That's why you need the fourth and final

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:19.680
step. Replace your stun double with the

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:22.959
real hero. Go after the real thing

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:25.600
directly. If you feel restless, write

00:16:22.959 --> 00:16:27.680
down what the pursuit was supposed to

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:30.560
give you. When you get to the top of the

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:33.199
hill, remember that all you're going to

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:36.079
see there is another bigger hill to

00:16:33.199 --> 00:16:38.720
climb. And you can still keep climbing,

00:16:36.079 --> 00:16:41.279
but have the clarity on why you're doing

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:43.440
that. If you feel behind, stop using the

00:16:41.279 --> 00:16:46.639
entire world as your comparison set.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:49.360
Compete with yourself. Define what good

00:16:46.639 --> 00:16:51.199
looks like to you for the life you're

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:53.360
actually living. So, those are the four

00:16:51.199 --> 00:16:56.000
symptoms. But you see that whichever one

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:58.720
that you're feeling, the move is the

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:01.279
same. It's the same four-step process.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:03.839
One clear definition of enough when

00:17:01.279 --> 00:17:06.319
you're restless, one race that you run

00:17:03.839 --> 00:17:09.520
against yourself when you're behind, one

00:17:06.319 --> 00:17:11.919
person who truly knows you, and one life

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:14.720
that changed because you were here. If

00:17:11.919 --> 00:17:17.760
you have those four things, there's not

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:20.160
much else that would matter.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:22.959
And if you don't have those, well,

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:26.559
there's still plenty of time. Modern

00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:29.919
life tells you happiness is waiting on

00:17:26.559 --> 00:17:32.559
the other side of success. It's like you

00:17:29.919 --> 00:17:35.919
see a a beautiful rainbow [music] and

00:17:32.559 --> 00:17:40.000
it's gorgeous. It's at a distance. So,

00:17:35.919 --> 00:17:42.320
you keep running like crazy toward it so

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:45.042
you can get close, so you can get to the

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:48.640
bottom of it, so you can touch it. But

00:17:45.042 --> 00:17:52.080
[music] you can run all day long and

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:55.039
you'll never get there ever because no

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:57.280
one does. The faster you move, the

00:17:55.039 --> 00:18:00.160
further it gets. [music]

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:03.360
And the funny thing is the light that

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:08.080
made the rainbow possible was coming

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:12.880
from behind you all this time.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.880
Thank you and I love you.

